WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:03.690
Lamp for reps. Part two: Engine leads.

2
00:00:04.210 --> 00:00:06.880
Where your calls come from, and how to work them.

3
00:00:07.180 --> 00:00:09.190
Click Engine leads.

4
00:00:12.860 --> 00:00:19.310
These are businesses our lead engine finds in public records. They're assigned to you. No other rep sees them.

5
00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:31.930
Tier is how strong the lead is. A means dial first. The small number beside it is need. Three is the strongest sign they need money now.

6
00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:41.890
Type is what kind of lead it is. A fleet, a contractor, an auto shop, or UCC, meaning a funder has filed on them before.

7
00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:47.670
Why is the reason it's on your list. Signals are the public records behind it.

8
00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:55.030
Status is where you stand. Set it after every call. It stamps the time, so the call counts in your numbers.

9
00:00:55.600 --> 00:01:01.290
Up top, filter by tier, status and type, or search by name, phone or city.

10
00:01:01.720 --> 00:01:03.470
Click a lead to open its page.

11
00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:12.490
Up top is the number to dial, and the status. Tap the number to call from your phone.

12
00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:17.170
Before you dial, read the Smart lead. It's your cheat sheet for this call.

13
00:01:17.530 --> 00:01:25.040
Their world this month tells you what's going on in their trade right now. A jeweler in November is stocking up for the holidays.

14
00:01:25.580 --> 00:01:34.830
Why this lead tells you why to call now. Here, a building permit pulled thirteen days ago. The job is starting, and materials and crew get paid first.

15
00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:40.590
Open with is your first line, with their name and their trade. Copy it, or make it your own.

16
00:01:40.930 --> 00:01:45.600
Under it, the level they likely start at, and the one move that takes them up a level.

17
00:01:45.990 --> 00:01:52.360
Then who they are, how they'd use the money, the words they use, and what they'll push back with, with your answer.

18
00:01:52.790 --> 00:01:58.740
On the call, fill in what you got. Who you spoke to, their email, their best number, and your notes.

19
00:01:59.270 --> 00:02:08.440
No time to type? Tap Speak and just talk. Lamp writes your notes for you. Tap Stop when you're done.

20
00:02:08.820 --> 00:02:14.630
Ready to apply? Start application opens their paper application in a new tab.

21
00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:22.870
You fill it in with them, on the phone. It saves to Lamp as you go. Skip the Social Security number and date of birth. They add those.

22
00:02:23.350 --> 00:02:31.340
At the end, email it or text it to them. They check it, add their private numbers, and sign. It lands on your board.

23
00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:37.710
Or press Send the application, to email or text them their link without filling it in.

24
00:02:38.070 --> 00:02:40.460
Sound like you know their business, because you do.

25
00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:46.810
Your target. 20 live conversations a day. Not dials. Conversations.

26
00:02:47.530 --> 00:02:50.460
Next: your files, stage by stage.
